TERMS AND CONDITIONS

Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person or organization
obtaining a copy of this software and associated documentation files (the
"Work"), to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or
sell copies of the Work, subject to the following conditions:

1. ATTRIBUTION (Sacred Acknowledgment)

   All copies or substantial portions of the Work must include:

   a) This license notice in full
   b) Copyright notice: "Original work by Tristan Stoltz / Luminous Dynamics"
   c) Link to source: https://github.com/Luminous-Dynamics/infin-love
   d) Recognition that this work is based on sacred reciprocity principles

   Attribution honors the flow of gifts and maintains the lineage of creation.

2. SACRED INTENTION (Purpose Alignment)

   The Work may be used for any lawful purpose that does not fundamentally
   contradict the principles of sacred reciprocity, including but not limited to:

   ✓ Personal, educational, or research use
   ✓ Non-profit and charitable organizations
   ✓ Commercial use that honors ethical business practices
   ✓ Derivative works that maintain or enhance accessibility
   ✓ Community building and gift economy initiatives

   The Work shall NOT be used for:

   ✗ Exploitation, manipulation, or harm of individuals or communities
   ✗ Deliberate creation of barriers to accessibility
   ✗ Removal of attribution or misrepresentation of origin
   ✗ Violation of human dignity or rights
   ✗ Purposes fundamentally opposed to sacred reciprocity values

3. ACCESSIBILITY (Universal Access)

   Any public-facing derivative work must:

   a) Maintain or improve accessibility for persons with disabilities
   b) Strive for WCAG 2.1 AA compliance at minimum
   c) Not create unnecessary barriers to access
   d) Honor the principle that all beings deserve access to sacred spaces

4. SHARE-ALIKE (Gift Flow Continuation)

   Derivative works that are distributed publicly must be:

   a) Made available under this same Sacred Commons License, OR
   b) A compatible open source license (MIT, Apache 2.0, GPL, etc.)
   c) With clear attribution to the original work

   This ensures the gift continues to flow while allowing practical flexibility.

5. COMMERCIAL USE (Ethical Exchange)

   Commercial use is permitted under these guidelines:

   a) You may charge for services, hosting, customization, or support
   b) You may integrate this work into commercial products
   c) You should consider voluntary reciprocity to support maintenance
   d) You must maintain attribution and license notices
   e) Large commercial entities are encouraged to contribute back financially

   Commercial success and sacred reciprocity can coexist in balance.

6. MODIFICATION (Creative Adaptation)

   You are free to:

   a) Modify the Work for your own use
   b) Adapt it to your community's needs
   c) Translate it to other languages
   d) Create derivative works

   With the understanding that:

   - Attribution remains required
   - Core accessibility must be maintained
   - The sacred intention should be honored
   - Modifications that improve accessibility are celebrated

7. NO WARRANTY (As-Is Offering)

   THE WORK IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
   AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
   LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
   OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE WORK OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
   WORK.

   This work is offered as a gift. Gifts come without guarantees, but with
   good intention.

8. TERMINATION (Sacred Boundaries)

   Your rights under this license terminate automatically if you:

   a) Violate any of the terms outlined above
   b) Use the Work in ways fundamentally opposed to sacred reciprocity
   c) Deliberately remove attribution or misrepresent authorship
   d) Create barriers that prevent accessibility for marginalized communities

   Termination does not affect the rights of those who received the Work from
   you under this license, provided they remain in compliance.

9. INTERPRETATION (Spirit Over Letter)

   This license should be interpreted in the spirit of sacred reciprocity:

   - Assume good faith when possible
   - Prioritize collaboration over litigation
   - Seek dialogue before enforcement
   - Honor both rights and responsibilities
   - Balance freedom with integrity

   When in doubt, ask: "Does this action support the flow of gifts?"

